   "source": [
    "# Make your first API call"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "3db82b61",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "An **API** (Application Programming Interface) is a way for two computer programs to talk to each other.\n",
      "\n",
      "Think of it like a **restaurant menu**:\n",
      "\n",
      "- You don’t go into the kitchen and cook the food yourself.\n",
      "- You choose something from the menu.\n",
      "- The waiter takes your request to the kitchen.\n",
      "- The kitchen prepares it and sends it back.\n",
      "\n",
      "An API works similarly:\n",
      "\n",
      "- One app asks another app for something.\n",
      "- The API tells the app what requests are allowed.\n",
      "- The other app sends back the result.\n",
      "\n",
      "For example, a weather app might use an API to ask a weather service:  \n",
      "**“What’s the weather in London?”**\n",
      "\n",
      "The weather service replies with the temperature, forecast, and other details.\n",
      "\n",
      "So, in simple terms:  \n",
      "**An API is a set of rules that lets apps request and share information with each other.**\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from openai import OpenAI\n",
    "\n",
    "client = OpenAI()\n",
    "\n",
    "response = client.responses.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-5.5\",\n",
    "    input=\"Explain what an API is in simple English\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(response.output_text)"
   ]
  }
